  "worked_solution": "In each instance of the game, there are three possible outcomes for $X$:\n\n* The result $X=-6$ occurs $3$ times out of $9$ in the payoff matrix. Therefore the corresponding probability is $\\frac{3}{9}=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\n* The result $X=-2$ occurs $3$ times out of $9$ in the payoff matrix. Therefore the corresponding probability is $\\frac{3}{9}=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\n* The result $X=6$ occurs $3$ times out of $9$ in the payoff matrix. Therefore the corresponding probability is $\\frac{3}{9}=\\frac{1}{3}.$\n\nHence, the probability mass function for $X$ is\n\n| $X$ | $-6$ | $-2$ | $6$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $f(X)$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ | $\\frac{1}{3}$ |\n\nHence, $q=r=\\frac{1}{3}.$",
